1
00:00:01,105 --> 00:00:02,065
Let's part ways.

2
00:00:03,505 --> 00:00:05,105
I don't think I can do this anymore.

3
00:00:05,185 --> 00:00:07,305
<i>If someone betrayed you,</i>
<i>what would you do?</i>

4
00:00:07,385 --> 00:00:09,985
<i>You keep forgiving people.</i>
<i>When are you ever going to get revenge?</i>

5
00:00:10,065 --> 00:00:12,665
<i>A presto amora!</i>

6
00:00:12,745 --> 00:00:13,945
<i>Wait.</i>

7
00:00:14,025 --> 00:00:15,145
<i>Why do you have this pen?</i>

8
00:00:15,225 --> 00:00:16,265
This pen?

9
00:00:17,105 --> 00:00:18,025
Well, it's mine.

10
00:00:19,105 --> 00:00:20,465
Rin!

11
00:00:25,625 --> 00:00:26,705
You're still alive.

12
00:00:33,985 --> 00:00:34,945
Here.

13
00:00:38,465 --> 00:00:39,305
Thanks.

14
00:00:41,465 --> 00:00:45,345
So now are you going to tell me
why you suddenly showed up like that?

15
00:00:54,505 --> 00:00:56,025
I thought you'd been run over, you know?

16
00:00:56,105 --> 00:00:57,585
Me?

17
00:00:58,305 --> 00:01:00,745
Weren't you the one who almost got hit?

18
00:01:08,145 --> 00:01:10,665
But nothing else unlucky
happened to you today, right?

19
00:01:12,385 --> 00:01:14,945
Today? Not really.

20
00:01:16,105 --> 00:01:19,425
I just fell over a little this morning.

21
00:01:19,505 --> 00:01:21,185
My motorcycle ran out of gas,

22
00:01:21,265 --> 00:01:22,825
and someone spilled orange juice
all over my shirt.

23
00:01:22,905 --> 00:01:24,265
It was a damn mess.

24
00:01:24,345 --> 00:01:25,705
That's why I had to change into this.

25
00:01:26,305 --> 00:01:27,145
That's all.

26
00:01:28,785 --> 00:01:31,225
Yeah, exactly.
Everything that happened was unlucky.

27
00:01:32,025 --> 00:01:34,305
Hey. Do you want to go make merit with me?

28
00:01:34,385 --> 00:01:35,745
Come on. Let me take you.

29
00:01:36,905 --> 00:01:37,905
No.

30
00:01:37,985 --> 00:01:40,065
I don't care about that stuff.

31
00:01:58,945 --> 00:02:00,385
<i>Huh? What?</i>

32
00:02:00,465 --> 00:02:03,185
The heir to our family's mystical lineage?

33
00:02:08,144 --> 00:02:09,864
Hello, Grandma.

34
00:02:09,945 --> 00:02:11,785
Do you know where Mom is?

35
00:02:11,865 --> 00:02:14,945
"Mom"? Whose mom? My mom?

36
00:02:15,025 --> 00:02:17,465
Oh, my mom died ages ago!

37
00:02:17,545 --> 00:02:20,505
No, I mean my mom, Grandma.

38
00:02:20,585 --> 00:02:22,065
It's Rin, your grandson.

39
00:02:22,145 --> 00:02:23,945
Rin? Which Rin?

40
00:02:24,025 --> 00:02:24,985
I don't know you!

41
00:02:25,065 --> 00:02:26,025
It's this, Grandma.

42
00:02:26,105 --> 00:02:28,425
How do you break a curse
and stop someone from having bad luck?

43
00:02:28,505 --> 00:02:30,505
A crash? What is it?

44
00:02:30,585 --> 00:02:32,825
Not a crash, Grandma.
A curse! Curse, Grandma!

45
00:02:32,905 --> 00:02:34,705
What? Say it again.

46
00:02:34,785 --> 00:02:36,945
A curse.
Like cursing someone with bad luck.

47
00:02:37,025 --> 00:02:39,745
A crash?
I don't know what you're talking about.

48
00:02:39,825 --> 00:02:41,665
A curse, Grandma, not a crash!

49
00:02:41,745 --> 00:02:44,545
Crash this, crash that…
I don't know. I'm done talking.

50
00:02:44,625 --> 00:02:45,625
Grandma!

51
00:02:46,385 --> 00:02:47,345
Hey, Grandma?

52
00:02:49,505 --> 00:02:50,945
What the heck?

53
00:02:51,625 --> 00:02:53,145
Why are you yelling so loudly?

54
00:02:56,425 --> 00:02:57,905
Oh right.

55
00:02:57,985 --> 00:03:00,105
Did you accidentally throw away
this spellbook the other day?

56
00:03:00,985 --> 00:03:03,025
I found it, so I brought it back for you.

57
00:03:04,705 --> 00:03:07,265
Say thank you, little Rin!

58
00:03:08,505 --> 00:03:10,105
-You little bastard!
-Why?

59
00:03:10,185 --> 00:03:11,545
No. It won't get me.

60
00:03:12,185 --> 00:03:14,185
-It won't.
-Damn you!

61
00:03:15,545 --> 00:03:17,065
If you're upset, don't take it out on me.

62
00:03:17,145 --> 00:03:20,105
It's all your fault, you little shit!

63
00:03:20,185 --> 00:03:21,625
Don't use my bathroom again!

64
00:03:42,065 --> 00:03:44,665
IF THE CURSE IS NOT BROKEN
BEFORE THE CURSED PERSON'S BIRTHDAY,

65
00:03:44,745 --> 00:03:46,305
THAT PERSON WILL MEET THEIR END

66
00:03:48,585 --> 00:03:51,225
<i>How the hell am I supposed to know</i>
<i>when his birthday is?</i>

67
00:05:02,265 --> 00:05:03,105
Hey.

68
00:05:03,865 --> 00:05:07,425
I'm from the Faculty of Education.
I'm currently conducting some research.

69
00:05:07,505 --> 00:05:10,105
Could you fill out a questionnaire for me?

70
00:05:10,185 --> 00:05:12,065
I'm sorry. I'm really busy.

71
00:05:12,665 --> 00:05:14,505
Okay. No problem.

72
00:05:17,785 --> 00:05:19,345
Hey, wait.

73
00:05:19,425 --> 00:05:21,145
Could I take one copy
of the questionnaire?

74
00:05:21,225 --> 00:05:23,385
-I'll ask my friend to fill it out.
-Really?

75
00:05:25,625 --> 00:05:29,265
Once you've got the answers,
you can email them to me.

76
00:05:29,345 --> 00:05:33,705
Oh, and this is a little reward
for completing the questionnaire.

77
00:05:33,785 --> 00:05:34,945
Okay.

78
00:05:37,945 --> 00:05:39,105
Hello?

79
00:05:39,185 --> 00:05:42,865
Hey, calm down.
I'm working on it right now. I'm doing it.

80
00:05:42,945 --> 00:05:44,025
Relax, okay?

81
00:05:44,105 --> 00:05:46,745
Tell the professor it'll be
finished on time. It won't be late.

82
00:05:46,825 --> 00:05:49,065
Oh, Khobfa?

83
00:05:50,145 --> 00:05:52,105
Perfect. You're here.

84
00:05:52,185 --> 00:05:53,785
Help me fill out this questionnaire.

85
00:05:53,865 --> 00:05:55,545
I have to submit it this evening.

86
00:05:56,225 --> 00:05:57,505
Please.

87
00:05:59,345 --> 00:06:00,505
What questionnaire is this?

88
00:06:01,105 --> 00:06:03,705
You want to know?
Come on. Let's get started.

89
00:06:05,425 --> 00:06:06,945
Mr. Khobfa.

90
00:06:08,185 --> 00:06:10,145
How old are you? 20 or 21?

91
00:06:10,225 --> 00:06:11,865
I'm 20. I'm not 21 yet.

92
00:06:11,945 --> 00:06:14,145
So your birthday hasn't passed yet.

93
00:06:16,105 --> 00:06:17,385
What's your date of birth?

94
00:06:17,465 --> 00:06:19,345
Why do you need to know that?

95
00:06:20,825 --> 00:06:22,465
It's a personal identification question.

96
00:06:23,185 --> 00:06:24,025
Hurry up.

97
00:06:24,905 --> 00:06:26,265
August 20th.

98
00:06:26,345 --> 00:06:27,265
What year?

99
00:06:27,345 --> 00:06:28,825
2005.

100
00:06:29,425 --> 00:06:31,225
Okay. What time were you born?

101
00:06:31,305 --> 00:06:32,865
What does that mean?

102
00:06:32,945 --> 00:06:34,585
Your exact time of birth.

103
00:06:35,545 --> 00:06:38,345
What kind of questionnaire
asks for your time of birth?

104
00:06:39,025 --> 00:06:40,585
Just answer me.

105
00:06:43,465 --> 00:06:44,665
2:30 p.m.

106
00:06:45,745 --> 00:06:47,785
2:30 p.m.

107
00:06:47,865 --> 00:06:49,145
Okay.

108
00:06:54,465 --> 00:06:56,025
Is that the whole questionnaire?

109
00:06:56,105 --> 00:06:57,665
Those were only the basic questions.

110
00:06:58,945 --> 00:07:02,745
Oh right. Yeah. I completely forgot.

111
00:07:03,505 --> 00:07:05,425
Let's keep going.

112
00:07:07,705 --> 00:07:09,825
Okay. First question.

113
00:07:09,905 --> 00:07:12,465
At what age did you first have sex?

114
00:07:12,545 --> 00:07:13,545
What?

115
00:07:16,905 --> 00:07:18,145
Why are you so shocked?

116
00:07:18,825 --> 00:07:20,665
It's just a basic question.

117
00:07:20,745 --> 00:07:22,505
Answer it. Don't think too much.

118
00:07:23,625 --> 00:07:25,105
Can I ask you the same thing?

119
00:07:25,785 --> 00:07:27,545
At what age did you first have sex?

120
00:07:30,425 --> 00:07:33,425
If you tell me, I'll tell you mine.

121
00:07:36,025 --> 00:07:38,145
Hurry up. It's only a basic question.

122
00:07:38,225 --> 00:07:40,145
It shouldn't be difficult
to answer, should it?

123
00:07:43,785 --> 00:07:45,225
I've never done it.

124
00:07:45,785 --> 00:07:46,905
Jeez.

125
00:07:49,665 --> 00:07:51,665
Well, now it's your turn.

126
00:07:55,585 --> 00:07:56,585
Never.

127
00:07:58,545 --> 00:08:00,785
What's with that look on your face?

128
00:08:01,385 --> 00:08:03,305
Just write it down.

129
00:08:03,385 --> 00:08:04,745
"Never."

130
00:08:10,385 --> 00:08:11,865
Can I believe you?

131
00:08:14,065 --> 00:08:15,225
One hundred percent.

132
00:08:21,585 --> 00:08:22,585
Okay.

133
00:08:27,225 --> 00:08:28,585
Oh, I almost forgot.

134
00:08:28,665 --> 00:08:31,505
Your reward
for completing the questionnaire.

135
00:08:33,664 --> 00:08:34,825
-Shit!
-Shit!

136
00:08:37,784 --> 00:08:40,305
You haven't done it yet,
but you will someday.

137
00:08:40,385 --> 00:08:41,865
Keep it for later.

138
00:09:04,785 --> 00:09:06,385
His birthday is in three months.

139
00:09:08,145 --> 00:09:10,505
What am I supposed to do next?

140
00:09:18,785 --> 00:09:20,065
There are witches too?

141
00:09:25,025 --> 00:09:27,425
Damn, this stuff is scary.

142
00:09:34,105 --> 00:09:36,865
HOW TO BREAK A CURSE

143
00:09:41,385 --> 00:09:43,185
10 WAYS TO BREAK
BLACK MAGIC AND DARK SPELLS

144
00:09:43,265 --> 00:09:44,545
BREAKING THE "CURSED FATE"

145
00:09:46,505 --> 00:09:47,905
Why are there so many?

146
00:09:52,225 --> 00:09:56,785
AI, could you summarize which method
of breaking a curse works best?

147
00:09:57,425 --> 00:09:59,905
<i>Certainly.</i>
<i>It depends on what you believe in.</i>

148
00:09:59,985 --> 00:10:02,185
<i>Many different methods</i>
<i>are commonly discussed</i>

149
00:10:02,265 --> 00:10:06,545
<i>in online communities related</i>
<i>to spiritual beliefs and superstition.</i>

150
00:10:08,185 --> 00:10:10,745
Then could you give me
the most reliable one?

151
00:10:14,705 --> 00:10:17,945
<i>I recommend MUNIVERSE on OpenChat.</i>

152
00:10:18,025 --> 00:10:23,305
<i>It has tens of thousands of members</i>
<i>and a reliability rating of 98.9%.</i>

153
00:10:27,545 --> 00:10:28,825
MUNIVERSE?

154
00:10:43,025 --> 00:10:47,065
WHY DID YOU JOIN MUNIVERSE?

155
00:10:47,145 --> 00:10:48,825
<i>I'm looking for a way to break a curse.</i>

156
00:10:55,385 --> 00:10:58,185
<i>I found my cat</i>
<i>after it had been missing for days.</i>

157
00:10:58,265 --> 00:10:59,785
<i>Thank you so much, everyone,</i>

158
00:10:59,865 --> 00:11:02,785
<i>for suggesting that I use</i>
<i>Khaitoon's photo to make a wish.</i>

159
00:11:02,865 --> 00:11:05,985
<i>You're welcome. I'm so happy for you.</i>

160
00:11:13,385 --> 00:11:17,145
<i>If we accidentally cursed someone</i>
<i>and caused them to have bad luck,</i>

161
00:11:17,225 --> 00:11:19,505
<i>what should we do</i>
<i>to make their bad luck disappear?</i>

162
00:11:22,425 --> 00:11:25,145
<i>Take the person to a ritual</i>
<i>to ward off their bad luck.</i>

163
00:11:33,185 --> 00:11:35,145
<i>Is there another way?</i>

164
00:11:35,225 --> 00:11:37,385
<i>I don't think he'd ever agree</i>
<i>to go with me.</i>

165
00:11:43,465 --> 00:11:47,225
<i>Then try using his photo</i>
<i>to pray to something sacred instead.</i>

166
00:11:51,985 --> 00:11:53,345
A photo?

167
00:12:12,225 --> 00:12:13,705
He's secretly stalking a guy.

168
00:12:13,785 --> 00:12:15,505
Yeah, he's so boy crazy.

169
00:12:16,545 --> 00:12:19,265
Hey, wait. No, that's not it!

170
00:12:19,345 --> 00:12:21,345
Isn't this a PDPA violation?

171
00:12:29,505 --> 00:12:30,585
Huh?

172
00:12:31,545 --> 00:12:32,745
Damn it.

173
00:12:42,345 --> 00:12:43,425
YOUNG ENTREPRENEURS

174
00:13:14,945 --> 00:13:18,305
So you're the one who played that guitar?

175
00:13:50,985 --> 00:13:54,065
Hey, what the hell are you doing?

176
00:13:58,025 --> 00:13:59,705
Well…

177
00:13:59,785 --> 00:14:02,785
I'm taking pictures of flowers. I have
to sketch and submit it to my professor.

178
00:14:08,305 --> 00:14:09,425
Fake flowers?

179
00:14:10,865 --> 00:14:13,585
Fake flowers are still flowers anyway.

180
00:14:13,665 --> 00:14:14,785
Really?

181
00:14:16,225 --> 00:14:18,985
I got the pictures. I'm leaving.

182
00:14:28,945 --> 00:14:31,185
Let me make a wish.
Khobfa, the person in this photo…

183
00:14:31,265 --> 00:14:34,625
Please keep him safe.
Let only good things happen to him.

184
00:14:35,225 --> 00:14:37,385
Don't let him experience
any more bad luck.

185
00:14:37,465 --> 00:14:39,345
Please make the curse of bad luck
I placed on him…

186
00:14:41,305 --> 00:14:43,185
disappear!

187
00:14:55,305 --> 00:14:57,905
<i>I've already tried using his photo</i>
<i>to pray to something sacred.</i>

188
00:14:57,985 --> 00:15:00,425
<i>All right.</i>
<i>Let's wait and see what happens.</i>

189
00:15:00,505 --> 00:15:01,905
<i>Good luck.</i>

190
00:15:03,585 --> 00:15:06,945
Sacred spirits, sacred spirits,
please help me.

191
00:15:10,225 --> 00:15:12,585
-My dear friend Rin.
-Yes?

192
00:15:12,665 --> 00:15:15,065
Do you want to go
to the movies with us tomorrow?

193
00:15:15,145 --> 00:15:18,505
After the movie, how about karaoke?

194
00:15:18,585 --> 00:15:22,425
<i>-Love, love, I need somebody to love</i>
<i>-Love, love, I need somebody to love</i>

195
00:15:22,505 --> 00:15:25,265
Well, I really want to go with you guys,

196
00:15:25,345 --> 00:15:28,385
but I have something to take care of.

197
00:15:28,465 --> 00:15:30,185
Maybe next time.

198
00:15:32,185 --> 00:15:33,825
You're always like this.

199
00:15:35,265 --> 00:15:39,585
Come on. Once I finish dealing with this,
I will get my freedom back.

200
00:15:40,785 --> 00:15:42,465
What are you dealing with?

201
00:15:43,665 --> 00:15:46,465
Well, I have to…

202
00:15:47,225 --> 00:15:50,865
<i>-Love, love, I need somebody to love</i>
<i>-I need somebody to love</i>

203
00:15:51,945 --> 00:15:55,505
<i>But that person must be you</i>

204
00:15:55,585 --> 00:15:58,585
-Why didn't you continue singing with me?
-I don't know the lyrics.

205
00:16:15,225 --> 00:16:16,705
The target is currently safe.

206
00:16:16,785 --> 00:16:18,225
I'll continue monitoring him.

207
00:16:23,505 --> 00:16:24,865
SOLD OUT!

208
00:16:30,505 --> 00:16:32,345
Is he seriously still having bad luck?

209
00:16:32,425 --> 00:16:34,785
<i>That's normal.</i>
<i>I'd recommend waiting a little longer.</i>

210
00:16:34,865 --> 00:16:35,985
Maybe it was just a coincidence.

211
00:16:40,865 --> 00:16:43,905
Shit. I don't think
this is a coincidence anymore.

212
00:16:48,585 --> 00:16:51,825
The target is on the move.
No signs of bad luck.

213
00:16:57,665 --> 00:16:58,985
-Shit!
-I'm sorry.

214
00:16:59,065 --> 00:17:00,905
-It's okay. I'm fine.
-Are you okay?

215
00:17:01,905 --> 00:17:03,665
He could've died from that!

216
00:17:06,385 --> 00:17:07,944
<i>It didn't work.</i>

217
00:17:08,025 --> 00:17:09,905
<i>I already prayed to something sacred,</i>

218
00:17:09,985 --> 00:17:12,145
<i>but he still keeps having</i>
<i>the same bad luck.</i>

219
00:17:12,224 --> 00:17:15,025
<i>Does anyone know</i>
<i>another method I could try?</i>

220
00:17:16,745 --> 00:17:18,424
<i>Try using holy water.</i>

221
00:17:18,505 --> 00:17:19,785
<i>They say that</i>

222
00:17:19,865 --> 00:17:23,224
<i>when someone has been cursed,</i>
<i>you should have them drink holy water.</i>

223
00:17:24,704 --> 00:17:29,225
<i>Holy water will make them</i>
<i>vomit out the evil inside them.</i>

224
00:17:33,665 --> 00:17:37,385
<i>This is holy water from a Buddhist temple,</i>
<i>and this is holy water from a church.</i>

225
00:17:59,345 --> 00:18:01,705
Mixing both together has to work!

226
00:18:23,305 --> 00:18:24,745
What is Rin doing there?

227
00:18:24,825 --> 00:18:26,385
There are plenty of other seats.

228
00:18:26,465 --> 00:18:28,345
Why are you sitting here?

229
00:18:28,425 --> 00:18:30,705
Can't I sit with you?

230
00:18:30,785 --> 00:18:34,425
Isn't he dating Khobfa just to spite you?

231
00:18:39,265 --> 00:18:41,225
Hey, did that person bring a cat to class?

232
00:18:43,465 --> 00:18:45,665
Whoa! That cat is huge.

233
00:18:54,065 --> 00:18:55,305
Where's the cat?

234
00:18:56,825 --> 00:18:58,385
What the hell is wrong with you?

235
00:19:01,665 --> 00:19:04,105
What are you eating? That looks good.

236
00:19:04,185 --> 00:19:05,305
None of your business.

237
00:19:23,025 --> 00:19:23,865
Hey.

238
00:19:24,625 --> 00:19:25,745
Hey, what's wrong?

239
00:19:26,505 --> 00:19:27,745
Hey.

240
00:19:28,425 --> 00:19:29,345
Spicy?

241
00:19:32,225 --> 00:19:34,625
Here. I bought you some water.

242
00:19:59,865 --> 00:20:01,105
I'm not drinking your water.

243
00:20:10,025 --> 00:20:10,985
Jeez.

244
00:20:17,225 --> 00:20:18,745
What am I supposed to do now?

245
00:20:40,785 --> 00:20:42,345
You don't have to do that
just to spite me.

246
00:20:45,145 --> 00:20:46,065
Spite you? How?

247
00:20:46,825 --> 00:20:50,105
Since when did you two get so close?

248
00:20:51,505 --> 00:20:52,705
We're in the same class.

249
00:20:55,065 --> 00:20:58,065
Khobfa isn't usually your type.

250
00:21:00,665 --> 00:21:02,785
And Krit is totally your type then?

251
00:21:04,705 --> 00:21:05,625
Mochi.

252
00:21:14,745 --> 00:21:16,185
If that's all, I'm leaving.

253
00:21:47,745 --> 00:21:48,785
I'm sorry about that.

254
00:21:50,705 --> 00:21:52,865
Rin hates you because of me.

255
00:22:08,745 --> 00:22:09,985
Are you okay?

256
00:22:10,585 --> 00:22:11,585
I'm okay.

257
00:22:14,105 --> 00:22:16,105
Did I make other people
think badly of you?

258
00:22:17,105 --> 00:22:18,745
I feel guilty.

259
00:22:19,625 --> 00:22:22,745
Forget about it.
I can't blame anyone for thinking that.

260
00:22:28,025 --> 00:22:28,865
Hey, wait.

261
00:22:39,505 --> 00:22:41,385
How can you still eat
so messily at your age?

262
00:22:47,105 --> 00:22:49,105
How am I supposed to eat this
without making a mess?

263
00:22:54,425 --> 00:22:55,265
Wipe it again.

264
00:22:56,265 --> 00:22:57,545
What are you, a baby?

265
00:22:58,265 --> 00:22:59,545
That sounds pretty cool.

266
00:23:04,145 --> 00:23:06,865
Whoa, didn't you just make it
even messier?

267
00:23:08,785 --> 00:23:11,065
In nature,

268
00:23:11,145 --> 00:23:14,305
every tree has a language of its own,

269
00:23:15,065 --> 00:23:18,425
and each tree grows at a different pace.

270
00:23:18,505 --> 00:23:22,385
Some trees need a long time
to establish deep roots,

271
00:23:22,465 --> 00:23:24,185
while others need less time.

272
00:23:24,265 --> 00:23:26,825
Do you know that
not every tree can survive?

273
00:23:26,905 --> 00:23:30,025
<i>Do you want to go make merit with me?</i>
<i>Come on. Let me take you.</i>

274
00:23:30,705 --> 00:23:31,705
No.

275
00:23:31,785 --> 00:23:33,505
I don't care about that stuff.

276
00:23:35,225 --> 00:23:36,105
-Shit!
-I'm sorry.

277
00:23:36,185 --> 00:23:37,345
-Are you okay?
-I'm fine.

278
00:23:44,465 --> 00:23:45,905
Do you know why it died?

279
00:23:46,545 --> 00:23:49,625
It wasn't an environmental problem
that killed the tree.

280
00:23:49,705 --> 00:23:56,065
It died because the person who planted it
accidentally hurt and killed it.

281
00:23:56,145 --> 00:23:59,145
It's the same with our relationships.

282
00:23:59,905 --> 00:24:05,305
Sometimes, we accidentally leave small,
invisible wounds on other people too.

283
00:24:05,985 --> 00:24:07,545
But the question is,

284
00:24:07,625 --> 00:24:11,065
does the caretaker
who accidentally damaged the branch

285
00:24:11,145 --> 00:24:13,425
still want to continue
taking care of the tree?

286
00:24:14,705 --> 00:24:19,425
Let's go back to the tree
whose branch we accidentally broke.

287
00:24:19,505 --> 00:24:21,585
Do you believe that if the caretaker…

288
00:24:21,665 --> 00:24:24,665
<i>I tried to get him to drink</i>
<i>the holy water, but he wouldn't.</i>

289
00:24:24,745 --> 00:24:26,105
<i>What should I do?</i>

290
00:24:28,865 --> 00:24:33,025
<i>Someone who isn't close to you</i>
<i>probably won't eat anything from you.</i>

291
00:24:33,105 --> 00:24:35,225
<i>Try getting closer to them first.</i>

292
00:24:35,305 --> 00:24:37,745
So today, I have an assignment
for all of you.

293
00:24:37,825 --> 00:24:40,025
This time, you'll be working in pairs.

294
00:24:40,105 --> 00:24:44,105
Therefore, everyone needs
to pair up today.

295
00:24:44,185 --> 00:24:48,265
You must submit your names to me
by the end of the day. Understood?

296
00:24:48,345 --> 00:24:50,785
-All right.
-Got it.

297
00:24:50,865 --> 00:24:52,745
Let's work together.

298
00:24:52,825 --> 00:24:54,225
Of course.

299
00:24:54,305 --> 00:24:57,385
Hey, what should the three of us do?

300
00:24:57,465 --> 00:24:59,145
Should we ask
if we can work as a group of three?

301
00:24:59,225 --> 00:25:00,345
Yeah.

302
00:25:00,425 --> 00:25:03,545
-Maybe we should ask him.
-Right.

303
00:25:03,625 --> 00:25:06,825
The person sitting next to me
refused to work with me. Shit.

304
00:25:08,105 --> 00:25:08,945
Hey.

305
00:25:10,345 --> 00:25:11,625
Do you see Khobfa?

306
00:25:12,465 --> 00:25:14,025
He just sits there looking miserable.

307
00:25:14,105 --> 00:25:17,385
Doesn't he care that
he doesn't have a partner to work with?

308
00:25:18,545 --> 00:25:19,465
That's weird.

309
00:25:21,425 --> 00:25:22,985
Okay, so the three of us
will work together.

310
00:25:23,065 --> 00:25:24,425
-Yeah.
-You come up with the topic.

311
00:25:24,505 --> 00:25:28,065
-Rin can write the report.
<i>-Try getting closer to them first.</i>

312
00:25:28,145 --> 00:25:28,985
Come on.

313
00:25:29,065 --> 00:25:31,905
Actually, I think you two should pair up.
I've got a partner already.

314
00:25:31,985 --> 00:25:33,225
-Huh?
-Huh?

315
00:25:34,585 --> 00:25:35,785
Hey, wait.

316
00:25:35,865 --> 00:25:37,345
-Hey.
-Rin?

317
00:25:38,025 --> 00:25:39,185
What the hell?

318
00:25:40,105 --> 00:25:41,825
-Khobfa.
-Shit!

319
00:25:41,905 --> 00:25:43,705
You don't have a partner
for the assignment, right?

320
00:25:43,785 --> 00:25:45,905
Neither do I. Let's pair up.

321
00:25:47,185 --> 00:25:49,185
I'm going to ask the professor
to let me work alone.

322
00:25:51,385 --> 00:25:52,545
Huh?

323
00:25:52,625 --> 00:25:55,665
Wait! Khobfa!

324
00:25:56,425 --> 00:25:58,785
If you work alone,
you might get unlucky again.

325
00:26:01,065 --> 00:26:02,625
I can take care of myself.

326
00:26:03,425 --> 00:26:04,345
Khobfa!

327
00:26:04,425 --> 00:26:06,305
Khobfa, are you okay?

328
00:26:07,345 --> 00:26:08,585
Are you okay?

329
00:26:10,665 --> 00:26:11,985
I'm fine.

330
00:26:13,065 --> 00:26:14,065
Ouch!

331
00:26:14,145 --> 00:26:15,345
Hey, be careful.

332
00:26:25,745 --> 00:26:26,865
Don't push yourself.

333
00:26:26,945 --> 00:26:28,105
Let's go to the infirmary.

334
00:26:30,385 --> 00:26:31,585
Get up.

335
00:26:37,945 --> 00:26:40,185
Walk slowly.

336
00:26:40,265 --> 00:26:43,025
STUDENTS MUST SIGN TO ACKNOWLEDGE RECEIPT
OF MEDICATION AND SERVICES

337
00:26:43,105 --> 00:26:44,305
Be careful for now.

338
00:26:44,385 --> 00:26:46,105
Don't walk too quickly,

339
00:26:46,185 --> 00:26:48,865
and apply a cold compress
three or four times a day.

340
00:26:48,945 --> 00:26:50,985
Don't forget to take the medicine
I gave you.

341
00:26:51,065 --> 00:26:52,465
-You'll recover faster.
-Thanks.

342
00:26:52,545 --> 00:26:54,105
-Thank you.
-Get well soon.

343
00:26:55,505 --> 00:26:57,505
Come on.

344
00:26:58,705 --> 00:26:59,705
Easy.

345
00:27:03,465 --> 00:27:04,305
Walk slowly.

346
00:27:05,145 --> 00:27:07,505
Wait here for now.
I already got you a ride.

347
00:27:08,185 --> 00:27:09,025
Huh?

348
00:27:09,785 --> 00:27:11,345
I'll ride my motorcycle home by myself.

349
00:27:11,425 --> 00:27:13,865
Your leg is injured. How can you ride?

350
00:27:13,945 --> 00:27:15,465
Absolutely not.

351
00:27:16,545 --> 00:27:17,505
It's arriving.

352
00:27:18,585 --> 00:27:19,425
Hey!

353
00:27:34,465 --> 00:27:36,665
No need. I'll open the door for you.

354
00:27:47,505 --> 00:27:48,345
Wait.

355
00:27:49,545 --> 00:27:50,505
What is it again?

356
00:27:50,585 --> 00:27:53,385
I'm going with you. How can you go alone?

357
00:27:53,465 --> 00:27:54,785
Move. Let me sit with you.

358
00:27:57,585 --> 00:27:58,505
Let's go, please.

359
00:28:17,425 --> 00:28:18,905
Take it slowly.

360
00:28:21,425 --> 00:28:23,105
You only need to take me this far.

361
00:28:23,785 --> 00:28:24,785
I can go by myself.

362
00:28:25,465 --> 00:28:27,185
How can you go alone?

363
00:28:27,265 --> 00:28:29,465
I said I can manage.

364
00:28:30,745 --> 00:28:31,745
Ouch.

365
00:28:31,825 --> 00:28:33,345
See?

366
00:28:43,025 --> 00:28:44,985
You never listen to me. See?

367
00:28:45,065 --> 00:28:46,825
Let me take you to your room.

368
00:28:49,665 --> 00:28:50,505
Come on.

369
00:28:52,865 --> 00:28:55,585
Don't put too much weight on it yet.
It won't get better if you do.

370
00:28:58,305 --> 00:28:59,625
You can manage, right?

371
00:28:59,705 --> 00:29:00,985
Yeah.

372
00:29:04,225 --> 00:29:05,705
Don't forget to apply
a cold compress often,

373
00:29:05,785 --> 00:29:06,825
and don't walk too much.

374
00:29:07,505 --> 00:29:11,225
Also, don't forget to take the painkillers
the nurse gave you. Got it?

375
00:29:14,745 --> 00:29:16,025
Oh.

376
00:29:16,105 --> 00:29:18,105
I ran out of water.

377
00:29:18,185 --> 00:29:19,865
Can I have some of yours?

378
00:29:26,945 --> 00:29:27,825
But…

379
00:29:27,905 --> 00:29:31,385
I've already drunk from this bottle.

380
00:29:31,465 --> 00:29:33,025
I don't mind.

381
00:30:01,585 --> 00:30:03,025
I'll…

382
00:30:04,065 --> 00:30:05,545
I'll do the report with you.

383
00:30:13,265 --> 00:30:14,105
Khobfa.

384
00:30:16,465 --> 00:30:17,305
Yeah?

385
00:30:17,985 --> 00:30:18,865
See you tomorrow.

386
00:30:20,425 --> 00:30:21,865
Get well soon.

387
00:30:45,705 --> 00:30:47,905
Yes!

388
00:30:47,985 --> 00:30:50,705
You drank the holy water.
Your bad luck will finally gone!

389
00:30:53,345 --> 00:30:54,985
This one is mine.

390
00:30:55,065 --> 00:30:56,505
I'll remember that.

391
00:30:59,545 --> 00:31:01,025
Hey.

392
00:31:01,105 --> 00:31:02,265
Rin.

393
00:31:10,745 --> 00:31:11,865
What's wrong with you?

394
00:31:12,625 --> 00:31:13,465
Nothing.

395
00:31:13,545 --> 00:31:15,865
Do you want to eat with us?
We bought a lot.

396
00:31:15,945 --> 00:31:18,225
-Yeah.
-You guys go ahead. I'm full.

397
00:31:19,465 --> 00:31:21,265
You already ate?

398
00:31:21,345 --> 00:31:22,265
Not yet.

399
00:31:23,545 --> 00:31:25,785
My heart is full.

400
00:31:26,745 --> 00:31:27,585
I'm going now.

401
00:31:28,265 --> 00:31:30,985
<i>You're such a darling</i>

402
00:31:31,065 --> 00:31:33,665
<i>You're not even trying</i>

403
00:31:33,745 --> 00:31:35,705
-His heart is full?
-Right.

404
00:31:39,985 --> 00:31:41,625
You're actually pretty cute.

405
00:31:43,425 --> 00:31:45,345
But you complain a little too much.

406
00:32:01,785 --> 00:32:03,425
<i>He drank the holy water.</i>

407
00:32:03,505 --> 00:32:05,305
<i>I think his bad luck is gone now.</i>

408
00:32:13,105 --> 00:32:14,985
I hope your bad luck is finally over.

409
00:32:40,225 --> 00:32:41,745
Krit, are you almost done?

410
00:32:41,825 --> 00:32:44,065
It's nearly time
for the live stream we announced.

411
00:32:44,865 --> 00:32:46,785
Give me a second. I'm almost done.

412
00:32:46,865 --> 00:32:48,065
Yeah.

413
00:32:53,545 --> 00:32:54,385
It's done.

414
00:32:57,185 --> 00:32:58,545
Come on. Let's go live.

415
00:33:15,305 --> 00:33:17,625
Your face is oily,
and your hair is a mess.

416
00:33:17,705 --> 00:33:18,905
Come. I'll fix it for you.

417
00:33:48,545 --> 00:33:51,585
What is it?

418
00:33:53,985 --> 00:33:54,825
Nothing.

419
00:33:56,145 --> 00:33:57,385
I like your eyes.

420
00:33:58,305 --> 00:33:59,545
They're pretty.

421
00:34:11,945 --> 00:34:13,505
Thanks.

422
00:34:15,585 --> 00:34:17,304
It's been a long time since anyone

423
00:34:17,945 --> 00:34:21,145
paid attention
to the little things about me.

424
00:34:44,505 --> 00:34:45,945
It's time to go live.

425
00:34:46,665 --> 00:34:48,665
-Let's do it.
-Yeah.

426
00:35:20,865 --> 00:35:22,825
RIN

427
00:35:30,305 --> 00:35:31,145
<i>Hello?</i>

428
00:35:31,825 --> 00:35:32,785
Are you awake?

429
00:35:34,225 --> 00:35:35,145
I'm awake.

430
00:35:36,545 --> 00:35:37,945
See you at the university today.

431
00:35:38,025 --> 00:35:39,865
We're meeting to work on the report.
Did you forget?

432
00:35:40,625 --> 00:35:41,745
No, I didn't.

433
00:35:41,825 --> 00:35:44,265
Do you want me to pick you up?

434
00:35:44,345 --> 00:35:47,025
No need. I'll take a car there myself.

435
00:35:47,105 --> 00:35:48,025
<i>Okay.</i>

436
00:35:48,705 --> 00:35:49,905
Be safe.

437
00:36:04,385 --> 00:36:05,345
Hello, Khobfa?

438
00:36:05,425 --> 00:36:06,585
Are you coming out yet?

439
00:36:06,665 --> 00:36:08,745
Yeah. I'm on my way.

440
00:36:11,385 --> 00:36:12,225
Hey!

441
00:36:13,305 --> 00:36:14,585
Khobfa!

442
00:36:14,665 --> 00:36:16,105
What's wrong, Khobfa?

443
00:36:19,505 --> 00:36:20,625
Hey!

444
00:36:21,585 --> 00:36:22,745
Shit.

445
00:36:22,825 --> 00:36:24,025
Rin. What?

446
00:36:24,105 --> 00:36:25,305
Rin!

447
00:36:25,385 --> 00:36:26,785
Where are you going?

448
00:36:35,465 --> 00:36:36,785
Khobfa!

449
00:36:42,705 --> 00:36:43,785
What happened?

450
00:36:45,065 --> 00:36:46,425
I'm sorry.

451
00:36:47,585 --> 00:36:51,585
I fell this morning,
so I went to buy some medicine.

452
00:36:53,505 --> 00:36:55,865
I should've picked you up from the start.

453
00:36:57,025 --> 00:36:58,385
It's okay.

454
00:36:59,385 --> 00:37:01,025
I'm not going to class today.

455
00:37:02,345 --> 00:37:05,025
Aren't you going to class?

456
00:37:06,905 --> 00:37:08,025
Forget it.

457
00:37:09,505 --> 00:37:11,025
Are you going straight to your room?

458
00:37:11,625 --> 00:37:14,705
Yeah. I'll head inside now.

459
00:37:20,625 --> 00:37:21,985
Give it to me. I'll help you.

460
00:37:41,465 --> 00:37:42,305
It's open.

461
00:37:59,785 --> 00:38:03,145
Why is it so hard to make one person
stop having bad luck?

462
00:38:04,065 --> 00:38:05,185
<i>Please calm down.</i>

463
00:38:05,265 --> 00:38:07,745
<i>It's normal for people</i>
<i>to go through periods of bad luck.</i>

464
00:38:07,825 --> 00:38:10,745
<i>Before long, the bad things</i>
<i>should pass on their own.</i>

465
00:38:10,825 --> 00:38:12,145
Yeah, that's true.

466
00:38:13,585 --> 00:38:16,305
I'll forget about it then.
I'll just pretend I have.

467
00:38:16,385 --> 00:38:17,705
No one will ever know.

468
00:38:18,385 --> 00:38:19,305
Know what?

469
00:38:20,385 --> 00:38:22,185
Were you talking to me just now?

470
00:38:22,265 --> 00:38:23,465
No.

471
00:38:23,545 --> 00:38:25,745
If there's anything I can help you with,

472
00:38:25,825 --> 00:38:27,825
just tell me.

473
00:38:27,905 --> 00:38:32,065
But today,
something really infuriating happened.

474
00:38:32,145 --> 00:38:34,945
Someone sent people to attack my friend,

475
00:38:35,025 --> 00:38:36,305
but they attacked the wrong person.

476
00:38:36,385 --> 00:38:38,305
-What?
-My friend got hurt for nothing.

477
00:38:38,385 --> 00:38:40,025
So how would you handle it?

478
00:38:40,105 --> 00:38:41,585
There was nothing I could do.

479
00:38:41,665 --> 00:38:44,825
As soon as they realized
the truth was out, they ran away.

480
00:38:44,905 --> 00:38:46,345
They're fucking awful.

481
00:38:46,425 --> 00:38:49,665
Yeah, now that you mention it,
that was really stupid of them.

482
00:38:49,745 --> 00:38:51,345
-Yeah.
-They even dragged others.

483
00:38:51,425 --> 00:38:52,905
How is your friend now?

484
00:38:52,985 --> 00:38:55,105
My friend isn't badly hurt.

485
00:38:55,185 --> 00:38:56,745
I'm just angry

486
00:38:56,825 --> 00:38:59,145
that they refuse to take responsibility.

487
00:38:59,225 --> 00:39:00,865
Don't you think they're assholes, Rin?

488
00:39:01,985 --> 00:39:03,505
They're assholes, right?

489
00:39:04,385 --> 00:39:06,425
Yeah. They're complete fucking assholes.

490
00:39:06,505 --> 00:39:08,105
They're the worst.

491
00:39:10,545 --> 00:39:12,305
When you do something wrong,
take responsibility.

492
00:39:12,385 --> 00:39:13,225
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

493
00:39:14,025 --> 00:39:15,025
-Assholes!
-Assholes!

494
00:39:15,105 --> 00:39:17,265
-Total assholes.
-Seriously.

495
00:39:17,345 --> 00:39:20,065
If I were you,
I'd go slap the hell out of them.

496
00:39:20,145 --> 00:39:22,825
I'd slap them left and right.

497
00:39:22,905 --> 00:39:24,705
I'd slap them from the front
and from behind for you.

498
00:39:24,785 --> 00:39:26,185
Let's go right now, okay?

499
00:39:26,265 --> 00:39:29,065
-Whatever you decide, I'm with you.
-I can't take it anymore.

500
00:39:29,145 --> 00:39:30,065
Let's go.

501
00:39:30,145 --> 00:39:31,945
MISSION: SAVE THE UNLUCKY ONE

502
00:39:32,025 --> 00:39:33,785
PHOTO
HOLY WATER

503
00:39:33,865 --> 00:39:35,505
These two methods didn't work.

504
00:39:36,505 --> 00:39:37,825
What the hell should I do now?

505
00:39:56,065 --> 00:39:57,465
A CURSE THAT LEADS TO ONE'S DOOM

506
00:40:01,025 --> 00:40:02,905
This is even worse
than cursing someone with bad luck.

507
00:40:03,505 --> 00:40:05,745
What the hell is this?

508
00:40:08,785 --> 00:40:10,385
MS. DARAN

509
00:40:14,905 --> 00:40:16,305
Mom!

510
00:40:16,385 --> 00:40:17,385
Mom.

511
00:40:18,065 --> 00:40:19,665
What are you doing, sweetheart?

512
00:40:19,745 --> 00:40:22,105
We haven't talked in ages.

513
00:40:22,625 --> 00:40:25,665
I just got a signal. How have you been?

514
00:40:25,745 --> 00:40:27,185
Mom.

515
00:40:27,265 --> 00:40:30,425
But what if I accidentally
used a curse from the spellbook

516
00:40:30,505 --> 00:40:31,905
to bring someone bad luck,

517
00:40:32,425 --> 00:40:34,185
but I don't know how to undo it?

518
00:40:34,265 --> 00:40:35,505
What should I do, Mom?

519
00:40:35,585 --> 00:40:37,465
Did you accidentally curse someone, Rin?

520
00:40:39,185 --> 00:40:41,065
Well, hypothetically, Mom.

521
00:40:41,865 --> 00:40:43,305
I didn't curse anyone.

522
00:40:43,385 --> 00:40:45,345
I'm just curious.

523
00:40:45,425 --> 00:40:49,585
I've never heard of a curse
that has absolutely no solution.

524
00:40:51,425 --> 00:40:54,665
Where there is white,
there must also be black.

525
00:40:55,705 --> 00:40:58,185
If there is night, there must also be day.

526
00:40:59,985 --> 00:41:02,025
I believe everything has a way out.

527
00:41:02,105 --> 00:41:04,785
You just haven't found it yet, Rin.

528
00:41:08,905 --> 00:41:10,305
But let me warn you.

529
00:41:10,385 --> 00:41:13,825
The stronger these things are,
the more careful you need to be.

530
00:41:13,905 --> 00:41:17,745
Don't use them recklessly
when you don't truly understand them.

531
00:41:20,785 --> 00:41:21,785
Got it.

532
00:41:22,825 --> 00:41:27,625
But did you accidentally curse someone?

533
00:41:29,105 --> 00:41:30,105
I didn't.

534
00:41:30,185 --> 00:41:31,465
That's all for now, Mom.

535
00:41:43,425 --> 00:41:45,185
Haven't found it?

536
00:41:56,185 --> 00:41:58,425
"Methods to balance misfortune."

537
00:42:03,065 --> 00:42:04,705
"If there be one cursed by misfortune,

538
00:42:05,265 --> 00:42:06,985
then must another of good fortune
be sought out."

539
00:42:08,905 --> 00:42:10,545
"The one of fortune

540
00:42:10,625 --> 00:42:12,985
must be born on the fifteenth waxing moon
of the sixth month,

541
00:42:14,585 --> 00:42:16,225
with the moon
as their ruling celestial body."

542
00:42:18,625 --> 00:42:20,385
Where do I find someone like that?

543
00:42:26,065 --> 00:42:28,705
AI, help me check my birth chart.

544
00:42:28,785 --> 00:42:31,745
I was born on May 17th, 2005.

545
00:42:31,825 --> 00:42:34,985
<i>You were born on the fifteenth night</i>
<i>of the sixth lunar month.</i>

546
00:42:35,065 --> 00:42:37,745
<i>Your ruling celestial body is the moon.</i>

547
00:42:37,825 --> 00:42:38,665
Yes!

548
00:42:39,265 --> 00:42:40,385
Finally!

549
00:42:40,465 --> 00:42:42,385
<i>Are you happy?</i>

550
00:42:42,465 --> 00:42:44,345
Yeah, I am.

551
00:42:44,425 --> 00:42:47,505
At least I'll finally be able
to save someone.

552
00:43:09,265 --> 00:43:10,825
Who's there?

553
00:43:21,345 --> 00:43:22,185
Who is it?

554
00:43:22,265 --> 00:43:24,625
-Yo, bro!
-Shit!

555
00:43:24,705 --> 00:43:25,905
Where did you come from?

556
00:43:25,985 --> 00:43:28,065
I've got good news for you.

557
00:43:28,145 --> 00:43:30,345
To make sure our report goes well

558
00:43:30,425 --> 00:43:32,385
and to keep you from getting hurt,

559
00:43:32,465 --> 00:43:36,145
from now on,
I'll pick you up for university every day.

560
00:43:37,265 --> 00:43:38,585
-Deal, okay?
-Hey!

561
00:43:59,225 --> 00:44:00,105
-Shit!
-Shit!

562
00:44:14,745 --> 00:44:16,665
<i>What am I supposed to do?</i>
<i>I can't be with him.</i>

563
00:44:16,745 --> 00:44:19,065
<i>I'm scared something unlucky</i>
<i>will happen to him again.</i>

564
00:44:19,145 --> 00:44:21,465
<i>Then you'll have to find a way</i>
<i>to stay with him 24 hours a day.</i>

565
00:44:21,545 --> 00:44:23,945
-Let me be your roommate, Khobfa.
-What?

566
00:44:24,025 --> 00:44:27,785
<i>If you make one shot out of five,</i>
<i>I'll let you be my roommate.</i>

567
00:44:27,865 --> 00:44:29,265
<i>You have to shoot with your eyes closed.</i>

568
00:44:29,345 --> 00:44:33,865
<i>I know you're busy,</i>
<i>but don't forget my birthday party.</i>

569
00:44:33,945 --> 00:44:36,825
It's not because I've met someone new.
You and I just can't be together anymore.

570
00:44:36,905 --> 00:44:38,185
<i>You've got it all wrong.</i>

571
00:44:38,265 --> 00:44:39,745
<i>Rin didn't come here to see you.</i>

572
00:44:39,825 --> 00:44:40,865
He came to see me.

